# GD-1 (round 19, writer 10): was L5_17_lots_two_sales. Its regime gains is unboxed (the items at top level, gains.x written x); the
# figures are unchanged. The comment below is the old test's.
# Round 18, C3-13 (follows, with two fixes beside it). L §5.17's lots example now orders `order b.day ties by (b.seq,
# s.day, s.seq)`. L5_17_regime_example with two lots bought on one day (buy1 10 units for 1 000.00 PLN, seq 1; buy2 10
# for 1 500.00 PLN, seq 2) and two sales of 6 units (sell1 on 2024-09-02, sell2 on 2024-10-01): the arcs in order
# (buy1; sell1), (buy1; sell2), (buy2; sell1), (buy2; sell2) take 6, 4, 0, 2 (first in, first out, L §5.12), so
# cost[sell1] = 6 · 100 = 600.00 PLN and cost[sell2] = 4 · 100 + 2 · 150 = 700.00 PLN. The old order line ties
# (buy1; sell1) and (buy1; sell2): RUN-TIE (L5_17_lots_two_sales_old_order). Beside it (writer 8, sixth pass):
# unit(q) of a quantity (L §5.10 Kind and unit), which the arc reads, was unbuilt (refcore read unit(x) of a place
# only, LOAD-UNIT); and taken of (buy2; sell1), a 0 with no key, now "takes the key of what it meets" (L §3.2) in
# cost's product and quotient (snap11 refused LOAD-UNIT `600 PLN and 0 PLN*notes/fund_x have different units`).
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2025-12-31
  start 2024-01-01
  end 2025-12-31

source pit_act "PIT act"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

kind persons
kind notes: unit
kind brokerages: place any min 0
kind ordinary: brokerages

kind trades: event certain
  leg units: notes
  leg cash: PLN
  attr seq: int
kind purchases: trades
kind sales: trades
  leg fee: PLN

kind assessments: event certain
  leg tax: PLN
input rate: num
input owner[x in brokerages]: key persons
place owed[p in persons]: debts PLN lives 2024-01-01..
place fisc: outside lives 1900-01-01..
fill matched[x in ordinary over ..]
  supply b.units.amount for b in purchases over .. where b.units.to == x
  demand s.units.amount for s in sales over .. where s.units.from == x
  arc b.day <= s.day and unit(b.units.amount) == unit(s.units.amount)
  order b.day ties by (b.seq, s.day, s.seq)
def cost[s in sales]: money PLN = round(sum(matched[s.units.from].taken[b, s] * b.cash.amount / b.units.amount for b in purchases over ..), minor(PLN), half-even) at s.day
def gain[s in sales]: money PLN = s.cash.amount - s.fee.amount - cost[s] at s.day
def tax[p in persons, y in years]: money PLN = round(sum(gain[s] for s in sales over y where s.units.from in ordinary and owner[s.units.from] == p) * rate, minor(PLN), half-up) at end_of(y)
move assess[y in years, p in persons on end_of(y)]: assessments
  on end_of(y)
  at end_of(y)
  leg tax from owed[p] to fisc amount tax[p, y]

version act_2024
  cite pit_act
  governs 2024..
  known 2023-12-01
  rate = 19 % "art. 30b"

source trades_log "own records"
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2019-01-01..
place market: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input t_day[k in trade_ids]: date
input t_units[k in trade_ids]: num
input t_cash[k in trade_ids]: money PLN
input t_fee[k in trade_ids]: money PLN
input t_seq[k in trade_ids]: int
index trade_ids = [b1, b2, s1, s2]

move buy1: purchases
  on t_day[b1]
  at t_day[b1]
  attr seq = t_seq[b1]
  leg units from market to mbank amount t_units[b1] * 1 fund_x
  leg cash from konto to market amount t_cash[b1]

move buy2: purchases
  on t_day[b2]
  at t_day[b2]
  attr seq = t_seq[b2]
  leg units from market to mbank amount t_units[b2] * 1 fund_x
  leg cash from konto to market amount t_cash[b2]

move sell1: sales
  on t_day[s1]
  at t_day[s1]
  attr seq = t_seq[s1]
  leg units from mbank to market amount t_units[s1] * 1 fund_x
  leg cash from market to konto amount t_cash[s1]
  leg fee from konto to market amount t_fee[s1]

move sell2: sales
  on t_day[s2]
  at t_day[s2]
  attr seq = t_seq[s2]
  leg units from mbank to market amount t_units[s2] * 1 fund_x
  leg cash from market to konto amount t_cash[s2]
  leg fee from konto to market amount t_fee[s2]

version own
  cite trades_log
  governs always
  known 2024-01-01
  persons + [ewa] lives 1980-01-01..
  notes + [fund_x] lives 2000-01-01..
  ordinary + [mbank] lives 2010-01-01..
  t_day[b1] = 2024-03-01
  t_day[b2] = 2024-03-01
  t_day[s1] = 2024-09-02
  t_day[s2] = 2024-10-01
  t_units[b1] = 10
  t_units[b2] = 10
  t_units[s1] = 6
  t_units[s2] = 6
  t_cash[b1] = 1 000.00 PLN
  t_cash[b2] = 1 500.00 PLN
  t_cash[s1] = 1 200.00 PLN
  t_cash[s2] = 1 300.00 PLN
  t_fee = 0 PLN
  t_seq = 1
  t_seq[b2] = 2
  owner[mbank] = ewa
  opening[konto] = 10 000.00 PLN at 2024-01-01 start "wyciąg"

ask c: cost[sell1], cost[sell2]
=== expect
c: (600.00 PLN, 700.00 PLN)
  unfulfilled: buy1
  unfulfilled: buy2
  cut 2025-12-31
